+## Lookup/getter proof attempt
+
+The partial fresh run is recorded in
+[`evidence/run-2026-10-05-map-lookup-getters/manifest.json`](evidence/run-2026-10-05-map-lookup-getters/manifest.json).
+It emitted the actual `HeaderMap::{find,find_with_hash,get,get_mut,get_all,contains_key}`
+bodies and actual `AsHeaderName::Sealed::find` implementations for
+`HeaderName`, `&HeaderName`, and `&str` under the named profile. A no-preprocess
+Why3 print found 43 direct roots across the 13 selected COMAs, with every
+proof JSON root set matching that print. The proof run exited 1: all seven
+`HeaderMap` body targets passed (7 own leaves and 23 call/spec support leaves),
+while the three sealed-key implementations and their three refinements have six
+open own leaves. The proof JSON trees report 18 successful own leaves and 30
+successful support leaves overall. Astra independently replayed the selected
+nested `split_vc` parents without a solver: all 13 archived COMAs and printer
+streams match, all 43 initial roots match the JSON roots, and every nested
+child arity matches. The audit records 24 own terminal obligations (18 passed,
+6 open) and 30 passed support leaves. This confirms tree completeness; it does
+not close the six open obligations. The durable details are in
